 ## Background
-The method, SLS4D, was introduced to address the limitations of dense voxel grids and direct coordinate-based interpolation in dynamic NeRFs. It builds on the D-NeRF [27] paradigm of using deformation fields but replaces the dense feature space with a sparse latent space. The work was published in IEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics in 2024 [S1]. It compares favorably to methods like T-NeRF, D-NeRF, TiNeuVox, K-Plane, HexPlane, and V4D [S1].
+The method, SLS4D, was introduced to address the limitations of dense voxel grids and direct coordinate-based methods in 4D novel view synthesis. It builds on the D-NeRF architecture by introducing a sparse latent space representation. The work was published in IEEE Transactions on Visualization and Computer Graphics in 2024 [S1]. It aims to reduce the computational burden and parameter count while maintaining high fidelity in dynamic scene reconstruction.
 
